1. The first unsupported implication being tested\n\nKeep the exact paired mass/log domain, complementary adjoint, composed\nDirac square, common heat prescription, fixed thermal period and regular\nbolt. Keep H, H_s, both original gravitational equations and every original\nmatching row. The preceding note proves complete thermal bounds for the\nAUXILIARY difference H_M,p-H_*,M,p. It does not identify its angular sum\nwith any independently renormalized part of the physical action.\n\nOne tempting next step is to sum that difference, apply the full H inverse,\nand bound the result separately from H_* minus the short comparison and\ncontacts. We test precisely that step. The actual physical common\nregulator is NOT replaced by a heat factor on the auxiliary scalar L_*.\nNo such auxiliary determinant exists in the argument.\n\nThe test uses compact smooth directions supported at .02<z<.03. These\nare genuine directions in the actual paired mass/log domain, with all\nouter phase coefficients zero and unchanged regular-bolt data. They are\nused to disprove a proposed bound on the whole domain, NOT as a replacement\ndomain or a choice of physical quantum source. Failure on this subset\nalready prevents that estimator from controlling the complete coupled\nsystem. The mass, quartic, correlated slow and interior columns cannot\nrepair a failed bound on an independent fast/interior direction.\n\n## 2. Exact operators and a controlled large-mass limit\n\nUse the predecessor's proper coordinate x, dz/dx=f=sqrt(Q), and\n\n    W=p/f, k^2=M^2+W^2,\n    t'=-2Wb, a'=2Mb, b'=2Ma-2Wt,\n    t^2+a^2-b^2=1, b(0)=0,\n    L=-partial_x(P partial_x)+V,\n    P=1/(Wa), V=4W/a+4Mt/a^2,\n    H_M,p=-Mt-4M^2 L^-1.                              (1)\n\nThe original auxiliary comparison uses the original graph cutoff chi:\n\n    P0=k/W^2, V0=4k^3/W^2, t0=M/k,\n    P_*=P+chi(P0-P), V_*=V+chi(V0-V),\n    H_*,M,p=-M[t+chi(t0-t)]-4M^2 L_*^-1.             (2)\n\nBoth scalar inverses have the actual Neumann seam value FREE and the\nactual finite-form regular-bolt branch. No wall is introduced. The cutoff\nis one on the test support; its entire transition is retained in L_*.\nThe predecessor's GLOBAL bounds L,L_* >= c M and relative form\n|L_*-L|<=1.85 K^-2 L, K^2=M^2+p^2/.17, remain available.\n\nLet p=M xi, w=xi/f, r=sqrt(1+w^2), and\n\n    B1=w'/(2r^3).\n\nFor xi in any fixed compact subinterval of (0,infinity), on nested compact\ncollars strictly inside 0<z<.05, the actual coefficient equations imply\n\n    b=B1/M+O(M^-3), b'=B1'/M+O(M^-3).                (3)\n\nHere is a justification with the actual endpoint return retained. The\nexact equation is A b=2W't, A=-partial_x^2+4k^2. The already proved bounds\nt-t0=O(M^-2) and (t-t0)'=O(M^-2) are uniform on these collars and xi\nintervals. For e=b-B1/M,\n\n    A e=2M w'(t-t0)+B1''/M=O(M^-1).\n\nThe positive Green comparison gives e=O(M^-3) on a smaller collar; the\nactual endpoint values contribute a polynomial in M times exp(-c M).\nThey are bounded from the actual Riccati cone and its first-order\nequations, not assigned zero. Differentiate the equation:\n\n    A e'=(A e)'-4M^2(r^2)'e=O(M^-1).\n\nIts forcing uses only the displayed bound on (t-t0)' and smooth seed jets\non these compact collars. The same nested comparison gives the second\nstatement in (3), including the exponentially damped endpoint values.\nThis argument is one-sided interior localization on the actual seed;\nit asserts no smooth extension of its cubic seam and no neighborhood\ntheorem. All O constants here are uniform for xi in the stated compact\ninterval, but are not numerical high-order coupled estimates.\n\nUse c=Wa+Mt and the exact identities\n\n    c^2=k^2(1+b^2)-b'^2/4,\n    a=(Wc+Mb'/2)/k^2, t=(Mc-Wb'/2)/k^2.\n\nEquations (3) give, with a0=w/r,\n\n    a/a0=1+alpha2/M^2+O(M^-4),\n    t=1/r+tau2/M^2+O(M^-4),\n    alpha2=B1^2/2+B1'/(2wr),\n    tau2=B1^2/(2r)-wB1'/(2r^2),\n    V/V0=1+v2/M^2+O(M^-4),\n    v2=-B1^2/2-B1'/(wr).                            (4)\n\nIn particular the potential correction and the tadpole MUST both be kept.\nFor compact smooth test functions u,v in the stated collar, the exact\nresolvent identity and (4) imply\n\n    M <v,(H_M,Mxi-H_*,M,Mxi)u> -> <v,d2(x,xi)u>,\n    d2=-(1+2w^2)B1^2/(2r^3)+w(w^2-1)B1'/(2r^4).   (5)\n\nThis is not a frozen-frequency replacement of the physical operator.\nTo check the inverse step, write V0=M Vbar, Vbar=4r^3/w^2. Substituting\nu/(M Vbar) in either actual scalar equation has compact residual O(M^-2).\nGlobal positivity then gives an L2 inverse error O(M^-3), and form-norm\nerror O(M^-5/2). Pair the exact identity\n\n    S-R=-R(L_*-L)S, R=L^-1, S=L_*^-1\n\nwith these approximations. Its potential term is v2/(M^3 Vbar); its\ngradient term is O(M^-5). The relative form bound controls the cross\nerrors by O(M^-5). Together with the tadpole this gives (5), with error\nO(M^-2) after multiplication by M. The inverses in this argument are\nglobal, so the cutoff transition and all regular-bolt/paired returns\nhave been retained. This also avoids estimating a termwise bolt C5 norm.\n\n## 3. COMPLETE discrete thermal sum, then the entire angular tail\n\nDefine at every angular mass\n\n    A_M=gamma sum_(j>=0)(H_M,pj-H_*,M,pj),\n    p_j=gamma(j+1/2).\n\nIts norm convergence was proved in the predecessor. That proof supplies\nthe uniform integrable envelope\n\n    ||M(H_M,Mxi-H_*,M,Mxi)||\n      <=2.752/(1+xi^2/.17)^(3/2)+.85/(1+xi^2/.17).   (6)\n\nThe actual mesh in xi is gamma/M. Uniform convergence on compact xi\nintervals follows from (3)-(5); the small interval next to zero is\nbounded by (6), and decreasing-envelope comparison controls its entire\nlarge-xi tail, including the lattice endpoint correction. Thus the\nCOMPLETE discrete thermal pairing, not selected frequencies, satisfies\n\n    lim_(M->infinity)<v,A_M u>=<v,C_aux(x)u>.         (7)\n\nNo thermal state has been replaced: the vanishing mesh occurs only in\nthis large-angular-mass limit with the original positive gamma fixed.\nBoth thermal signs enter the original action factor below. Nothing here\ninterchanges this sum with a common angular heat finite part.\n\nPut ell=-f'/f, so w'=ell w and w''=(ell'+ell^2)w. In (5), change the\ncontinuous integration variable xi to f w at fixed x. The two elementary\nintegrals are\n\n    int_0^infinity [-(1+2w^2)w^2/(8(1+w^2)^(9/2))\n                    -3w^4(w^2-1)/(4(1+w^2)^(9/2))] dw=-37/420,\n    int_0^infinity w^2(w^2-1)/(4(1+w^2)^(7/2)) dw=1/60.\n\nThey follow by w^2=t/(1-t) and the Euler beta integral with positive\nparameters ([DLMF 5.12.1](https://dlmf.nist.gov/5.12.E1)); that identity is\nused only for integrals, not as a domain or regulator theorem. Therefore\n\n    C_aux=f[ell'/60-ell^2/14]\n          =-f Q''/120-23(Q')^2/(1680f).              (8)\n\nThe last derivatives are in z. On the WHOLE interval .02<=z<=.03 the\nactual polynomial bounds give Q>.16, Q<.17, Q''<-.0775 and |Q'|<.0018.\nConsequently C_aux>2.58e-4 there. This nonzero term belongs to the\nauxiliary split, not to a newly selected physical contact.\n\nWith the exact angular masses M_n^2=n(n+q)/C and multiplicities\nd_n=2(q+2n), set D_N=sum_(n<=N)d_n=2qN+2N(N+1). Weighted Cesaro summation\nof (7) proves\n\n    D_N^-1 <v,sum_(n<=N)d_n A_Mn u> -> <v,C_aux u>.   (9)\n\nTake v=u nonzero. The positive right side proves divergence of this\nSEPARATE signed relative piece, not merely of its unsigned envelope.\nNo finite angular sample proves (9); it concerns the whole tail.\n\n## 4. The actual coupled inverse does not rescue this split\n\nThe original canonical source for these thermal pairs is\n-2G d_n A_Mn/(pi B^2 f). In z measure, (8)-(9) give the normalized source\nlimit in the shape row\n\n    J_aux(z)=G/(pi B^2)[Q''/60+23(Q')^2/(840Q)]\n             <-4.8e-47 on [.02,.03].               (10)\n\nThe trace row is zero for this quantum contribution, but both original\nrows of H are used by H^-1. If the images of these partial sources under\nthe actual coupled inverse were bounded in its energy space V, boundedness\nof H:V->V* would bound their pairing with the fixed admissible direction\n(0,u). Equation (10) makes that pairing grow in magnitude as D_N, a\ncontradiction. Equivalently,\n\n    liminf |<source_N,(0,u)>|/D_N\n       >=4.8e-47 ||u||_L2(dz)^2>0.                 (11)\n\nThis proves failure even with the global weak inverse and full domain.\nIt does not assign a numerical strong inverse norm or a finite N at which\na physical target is crossed. The source_N here tests a linear-operator\nestimator; it is NOT claimed to be the prescribed quantum residual or\nan actual correction. The full physical source is the COMMON combination\nof this piece with its companion comparison, original contacts, thermal\nand finite-domain returns. Its cancellation has not been evaluated.\n\n## 5. Quantified repair and unchanged coupled feasibility requirements\n\nDo not keep extending the separately summed auxiliary estimate. The\ncompanion H_* minus short-geodesic/contact allocation must cancel (8)\nwithin the ORIGINAL composed-square common regulator, before separate\nangular norms or a physical interpretation. Adding and subtracting (8)\nalgebraically is allowed; discarding it or choosing a new finite contact\nis not. Its computed value fixes a check on the required matching.\n\nRemoving only a constant angular asymptote is not a summability proof.\nA residual M^-2 bound still has sum d_n/M_n^2=infinity (asymptotic 4C/n).\nAn absolute estimate must decay faster than M^-2; a convenient explicit\ngoal is M^-4 after the matched local terms through order M^-2 are retained.\nThen the exact entire-tower bound is\n\n    sum_(n>=1)d_n/M_n^4 <4C^2/q,\n    A4=(2G/(pi B^2))(4C^2/q)<4.583e-35.             (12)\n\nHere is a CONDITIONAL target in original units, not a changed norm.\nSuppose the complete commonly matched remainder satisfies, on the actual\nsource family, the ORIGINAL composed graph observation bound\n\n    ||T_old H^-1(0,f^-1 remainder_n[u])||H3\n                       <= C4 E(u)/M_n^4.           (13)\n\nThe inverse, density, phase extraction, quartic/slow/bolt matching and\ncutoff norms are included in C4. Equation (13) is UNKNOWN; the compact\nasymptotic test above does not prove it on the complete domain. It cannot\nbe obtained by relabelling the former L2 coefficient 1.686. All companion\nmatched local terms must also be evaluated and included in the ledger.\nNo numerical value of C4, or of any phase-column input norm, is assumed.\n\nFor affine energy <=1.1e-10, this remainder alone would fit the remaining\naffine allowance if C4<=1e33: (12) gives <=5.0413e-12. That leaves only\n>3.0104999994957e-13 for the OTHER unallocated affine entries. The exact\nsole-entry ceiling is the actual residual divided by A4*(1.1e-10),\napproximately 1.06e33. It is an allowance, not a computed coefficient.\nFor feedback the corresponding complete condition would include\n\n    eta_other+(.0195239+4.583e-13+A4*C4) gamma_E <.0012069. (14)\n\nEven gamma_E is UNKNOWN on the actual source family. For arbitrary\nouter-data-only inputs no such comparison exists, as previously proved.\nThe allowance C4=1e33 contributes at most .04583 gamma_E; with eta_other=0\nthe conservative ceiling is gamma_E<.01846. These are explicit sufficient\nalternative targets, not evidence that either is attainable. The actual\nother matched terms and column norms remain necessary; no remaining\nentry has been assumed to fit.\n\nThe exact reference mass lift remains J_m=int_0^z t^3/Q^2,\nn_m=-2beta QJ_m/z, b_m=beta z^3/Q+beta Q'J_m. Both local reference rows\ncancel. Its original transition remains\nf_cut=2xz chi_m-2F n_m Dchi_m and alpha_cut=n_m Dchi_m; its reference bolt\nshift is zero and net mass is -xB. It is not a global fixed-temperature\nzero mode. Its original-fast conversion >.00906808164|m| remains, so\nboth 1e-11 graph ceilings require actual |m|<2.20553814952e-9.\n\nNeither actual m nor kappa_m is evaluated. IF kappa_m<=5e-5, its affine,\ngraph and independent-energy debits are 2.14765e-12, .0024731 and .0195239.\nAfter the controlled far entry the residual affine allowance is\n5.34234999994958e-12. The scalar quartic's ORIGINAL second-row coefficient\n20 beta Fstar, the exact correlated slow pair and every Schur coupling\nare still present and UNKNOWN. The original mass moment remains an exact\ncompatibility equation, not a tolerance.\n\nThe quantum-fast screen .028913+1e-11(1.0706e10)=.135973<.1599164 retains\nonly its two-fast-input admitted-family scope. Original physical-norm\nand neighborhood comparisons remain unproved. In particular, with rho=1e-8,\n\n    E_center+1e-8 alpha<=1e-11,\n    R_X alpha*.028913+Z0_other<=.25,\n    R_X alpha^2*1.0706e10+Z2_other<=5e7,\n    Y0+1e-8 Z0+5e-17 Z2<=1e-8, Z0+1e-8 Z2<1\n\nare not closed by this test. Independent boundary-phase variations are\nnot controlled by a fast-input screen. Compatibility, physical matching,\nsemiclassical validity/noise and all-sector stability remain unresolved.\n\nEXECUTED: the full signed auxiliary response's large-angular-mass limit\nafter its complete discrete thermal sum; its nonzero coefficient and\noriginal-unit sign on an actual-domain interval; the failure of separately\nsumming that piece even after the full coupled weak inverse; and numerical\ntargets for a specified commonly matched M^-4 alternative. Supporting\nsymbolic/interval checks verify algebra and bounds, not the continuum\nargument or a physical coupled solve.\n\nRESEARCH DECISION: keep the construction, but sharpen the method by\ncombining the auxiliary response with the original principal/contact\nallocation BEFORE angular estimation. Park separate angular estimates\nof H-H_*: their signed divergence has now been demonstrated. The full\nphysical coupled estimate remains unresolved, with no construction\nobstruction established and no actual controlled solution certified.\n\nONE NEXT CALCULATION (PROPOSED, NOT EXECUTED): compute the complete\ncommon-regulated coupled return with the companion terms matched through\norder M^-2, checking cancellation of (8), and certify its all-column\nM^-4 composed remainder (13) and signed retained terms against (14) and\nthe affine ledger. Include higher conormal derivatives and original\nmass/quartic/slow/bolt rows. The actual common-regulator error and the\nsigned coupled centers remain to be calculated; this test did not do so.\n\nRemaining to-do list: complete common-subtracted strong coupled return and\nsigned response; original physical-norm/neighborhood comparisons;\nnonlinear admission/contraction and exact compatibility; physical matching;\nsemiclassical validity/noise; all-sector stability; charge/return, opening,\ntransport, preparation, separate creation and the full stable semiclassical\nwormhole objective.\n", "checks/current_relative_angular_coupled_test.py": "\"\"\"Verify signed auxiliary asymptote and coupled estimator test; no physical solve.\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom hashlib import sha256\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom math import comb, factorial\nimport json, sys, traceback\nimport sympy as sp\nif '--arb-path' in sys.argv:\n    sys.path.insert(0,sys.argv[sys.argv.index('--arb-path')+1])\nimport flint\nfrom flint import arb,ctx\nctx.prec=512\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nSTEM='current-relative-angular-coupled-test'\nOWN=['notes/'+STEM+'.md','checks/current_relative_angular_coupled_test.py',\n     'evidence/'+STEM+'-review.json']\nsys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'checks'))\nsaved_argv=sys.argv[:];sys.argv=[sys.argv[0]]\nimport current_physical_york_dual_assembly as york\nsys.argv=saved_argv\nCHECKS=[]\n\ndef check(name,value,detail=None):\n    CHECKS.append(dict(name=name,passed=bool(value)))\n    if not value:raise AssertionError(name)\n\nyork.check=check;york.prior.check=check\n\ndef enc(v):\n    m,r,e=v.mid_rad_10exp(60)\n    return dict(ball=v.str(40),decimal_enclosure=dict(mid=str(m),rad=str(r),exponent=str(e)))\n\n\ndef execute():\n    par,horizon,zh,env=york.actual_parameters()\n    co={k:env[v] for k,v in zip(york.powers,york.qs)}\n    def deriv(j):\n        return {k-j:v*factorial(k)/factorial(k-j) for k,v in co.items() if k>=j}\n    def bern_interval(d,lo,hi):\n        n=max(d);a=arb(lo);width=arb(hi)-a\n        shifted={i:sum((d[k]*comb(k,i)*a**(k-i) for k in d if k>=i),arb(0)) for i in range(n+1)}\n        return [sum((shifted[i]*width**i*comb(k,i)/comb(n,i) for i in range(k+1)),arb(0)) for k in range(n+1)]\n    qb=bern_interval(co,'.02','.03')\n    qp=bern_interval(deriv(1),'.02','.03')\n    qpp=bern_interval(deriv(2),'.02','.03')\n    check('whole_actual_test_interval_Q_lower',all(v>arb('.16') for v in qb))\n    check('whole_actual_test_interval_Q_upper',all(v<arb('.17') for v in qb))\n    check('whole_actual_test_interval_Qprime',all(abs(v)<arb('.0018') for v in qp))\n    check('whole_actual_test_interval_Qsecond_negative',all(v<-arb('.0775') for v in qpp))\n    x=sp.symbols('x',real=True)\n    w=sp.Function('w')(x); rr=sp.sqrt(1+w*w)\n    B1=sp.diff(w,x)/(2*rr**3)\n    tau2=B1**2/(2*rr)-w*sp.diff(B1,x)/(2*rr**2)\n    alpha2=B1**2/2+sp.diff(B1,x)/(2*w*rr)\n    v2=-(w*w+2)/rr**2*alpha2+tau2/rr\n    check('relative_potential_subprincipal',sp.simplify(v2+B1**2/2+sp.diff(B1,x)/(w*rr))==0)\n    d2=-tau2+w*w*v2/rr**3\n    stated=-(1+2*w*w)*B1**2/(2*rr**3)+w*(w*w-1)*sp.diff(B1,x)/(2*rr**4)\n    check('complete_tadpole_plus_bubble_subprincipal',sp.simplify(d2-stated)==0)\n    ww,ll,lp=sp.symbols('w ell ellprime',real=True,positive=True)\n    d2poly=sp.simplify(stated.subs({sp.diff(w,x,2):(lp+ll**2)*w,sp.diff(w,x):ll*w,w:ww},simultaneous=True))\n    # Substitute in stages to ensure all functions are converted.\n    d2poly=sp.simplify(stated.subs({sp.diff(w,x,2):(lp+ll**2)*w,sp.diff(w,x):ll*w}).subs(w,ww))\n    a=-(1+2*ww**2)*ww**2/(8*(1+ww**2)**sp.Rational(9,2))-3*ww**4*(ww**2-1)/(4*(1+ww**2)**sp.Rational(9,2))\n    b=ww**2*(ww**2-1)/(4*(1+ww**2)**sp.Rational(7,2))\n    check('complete_integrand_decomposition',sp.simplify(d2poly-ll**2*a-(lp+ll**2)*b)==0)\n    ia=sp.integrate(a,(ww,0,sp.oo));ib=sp.integrate(b,(ww,0,sp.oo))\n    check('entire_scaled_thermal_first_integral',ia==-sp.Rational(37,420))\n    check('entire_scaled_thermal_second_integral',ib==sp.Rational(1,60))\n    check('full_thermal_local_coefficient',sp.expand(ll**2*ia+(lp+ll**2)*ib-lp/60+ll**2/14)==0)\n    z=sp.symbols('z',positive=True);Q=sp.Function('Q')(z);f=sp.sqrt(Q)\n    ell=-sp.diff(Q,z)/(2*f)\n    ellprime=f*sp.diff(ell,z)\n    caux=sp.simplify(f*(ellprime/60-ell**2/14))\n    formula=-f*sp.diff(Q,z,2)/120-23*sp.diff(Q,z)**2/(1680*f)\n    check('actual_geometry_conversion',sp.simplify(caux-formula)==0)\n    source=sp.simplify(-2*caux/f)\n    check('original_signed_source_density',sp.simplify(source-sp.diff(Q,z,2)/60-23*sp.diff(Q,z)**2/(840*Q))==0)\n    cmin=arb('.16').sqrt()*arb('.0775')/120-23*arb('.0018')**2/(1680*arb('.16').sqrt())\n    jmin=(arb('.0775')/60-23*arb('.0018')**2/(840*arb('.16')))/(arb.pi()*par['B2'])\n    check('nonzero_auxiliary_thermal_limit_whole_interval',cmin>arb('2.58e-4'))\n    check('nonzero_original_source_limit_whole_interval',jmin>arb('4.8e-47'))\n    n,N,q,C=sp.symbols('n N q C',positive=True,integer=True)\n    d=2*(q+2*n);mass2=n*(n+q)/C\n    dn=sp.summation(d,(n,1,N))\n    check('exact_all_angular_weight',sp.expand(dn-2*q*N-2*N*(N+1))==0)\n    check('angular_weight_diverges',sp.limit(dn,N,sp.oo)==sp.oo)\n    check('Mminus2_residual_is_borderline',sp.limit(n*d/mass2,n,sp.oo)==4*C)\n    check('Mminus4_summable_decay',sp.limit(n**3*d/mass2**2,n,sp.oo)==4*C*C)\n    # Established bound 4 C^2/q is conservative: compare decreasing F to integral.\n    xx=sp.symbols('xx',positive=True)\n    F=(q+2*xx)/(xx**2*(xx+q)**2)\n    check('mass_fourth_integral_antiderivative',sp.simplify(sp.diff(-1/(xx*(xx+q)),xx)-F)==0)\n    check('mass_fourth_decreasing_numerator',sp.simplify(-sp.diff(F,xx)*xx**3*(xx+q)**3-2*(q*q+3*q*xx+3*xx*xx))==0)\n    # Sum_{n>=1}F(n) <= F(1)+int_1^infty F < 2/q.\n    check('mass_fourth_complete_sum_guard',sp.simplify(2/q-(q+2)/(q+1)**2-1/(q+1)-(q+2)/(q*(q+1)**2))==0)\n    sum4=4*par['C']**2/par['q']\n    A4=2*sum4/(arb.pi()*par['B2'])\n    check('original_composed_angular_factor',A4<arb('4.583e-35'))\n    rem=arb('5.34235e-12')-arb('5.042e-23')\n    actual_ceiling=rem/(A4*arb('1.1e-10'))\n    affine_guard=arb('4.583e-35')*arb('1e33')*arb('1.1e-10')\n    check('alternative_affine_guard_exact',sp.Rational('4.583e-35')*sp.Rational('1e33')*sp.Rational('1.1e-10')==sp.Rational('5.0413e-12'))\n    check('alternative_other_affine_reserve',rem-affine_guard>arb('3.0104999994957e-13'))\n    ge=arb('.0012069')/(arb('.0195239')+arb('4.583e-13')+arb('.04583'))\n    check('alternative_feedback_sufficient_guard',arb('.01846')<ge)\n    check('conditional_fast_scope_numerical_screen',arb('.028913')+arb('1e-11')*arb('1.0706e10')<arb('.1599164'))\n    check('actual_temperature_is_positive_and_fixed',0<par['gamma']<arb('1e-33'))\n    return dict(outcome='unresolved_physical_coupled_estimate_with_verified_separate_signed_angular_estimator_failure',\n      signed_auxiliary_limit='-sqrt(Q)*Qsecond/120-23*Qprime^2/(1680*sqrt(Q))',\n      coefficient_lower_expression=enc(cmin),original_source_magnitude_lower_expression=enc(jmin),\n      whole_interval=['.02','.03'],all_thermal_integrals=[str(ia),str(ib)],\n      angular_weight='2qN+2N(N+1)',actual_sum4_upper=enc(sum4),original_composed_A4=enc(A4),\n      conditional_C4_sole_affine_ceiling=enc(actual_ceiling),\n      conditional_C4_selected_allowance='1e33',conditional_affine_remainder_guard=enc(affine_guard),\n      conditional_other_affine_reserve=enc(rem-affine_guard),conditional_gamma_E_ceiling=enc(ge),\n      actual_C4=None,actual_gamma_E=None,kappa_m=None,actual_mass=None,\n      signed_separate_piece_estimator_failure=True,actual_coupled_weak_inverse_does_not_remove_this_failure=True,\n      complete_thermal_asymptotic_executed=True,complete_angular_asymptotic_executed=True,\n      physical_common_regulator_limit_executed=False,common_subtracted_strong_sum_certified=False,\n      physical_coupled_signed_solve_executed=False,physical_operator_numerical_applications=0,\n      actual_paired_domain_retained=True,finite_mode_selection=False,all_coincidence_and_companion_terms_required=True,\n      actual_construction_obstruction=False,nonlinear_admission=False,nonlinear_contraction=False,\n      exact_compatibility=False,physical_matching=False,semiclassical_validity_noise=False,all_sector_stability=False,\n      full_objective_preserved=True,closed_audit_preserved=True)\n\nif __name__=='__main__':\n    mode='acceptance' if '--acceptance' in sys.argv else 'development'\n    out=ROOT/'evidence'/(STEM+('' if mode=='acceptance' else '-development')+'.json')\n    review=json.loads((ROOT/OWN[2]).read_bytes())\n    paths=set(OWN+review['retained_inputs'])\n    for module in list(sys.modules.values()):\n        f=getattr(module,'__file__',None)\n        if f:\n            try:rel=Path(f).resolve().relative_to(ROOT).as_posix()\n            except ValueError:continue\n            if rel.endswith('.py'):paths.add(rel)\n    digest=lambda p:sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    before={p:digest(ROOT/p) for p in sorted(paths)}\n    fr=Path(flint.__file__).resolve().parent\n    runtime=dict(python=sys.version,python_executable_sha256=digest(Path(sys.executable)),flint_version=flint.__version__,\n      flint_artifacts={p.relative_to(fr).as_posix():digest(p) for p in sorted(fr.rglob('*')) if p.is_file() and p.suffix in ['.py','.pyd','.dll']})\n    run=dict(started_utc=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),mode=mode,input_sha256_before=before,precision_bits=512,runtime=runtime,\n      frozen_sources_utf8={p:(ROOT/p).read_text(encoding='utf-8') for p in OWN})\n    try:\n        check('ordinary_argument_frozen',before[OWN[0]]==review['ordinary_argument_sha256'])\n        run['result']=execute()\n        run['input_sha256_after']={p:digest(ROOT/p) for p in before}\n        check('frozen_inputs_unchanged',before==run['input_sha256_after'])\n        run['status']='passed'\n    except Exception:run['status']='failed';run['traceback']=traceback.format_exc()\n    run['checks']=CHECKS;run['finished_utc']=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n    ledger=json.loads(out.read_bytes()) if out.exists() else {'runs':[]}\n    ledger['runs'].append(run);out.write_bytes((json.dumps(ledger,indent=2)+'\\n').encode())\n    with (ROOT/'evidence'/(STEM+'.log')).open('ab') as f:f.write((json.dumps(run)+'\\n').encode())\n    print(json.dumps(dict(mode=mode,status=run['status'],checks=len(CHECKS),result=run.get('result'),traceback=run.get('traceback')),indent=2))\n    if run['status']!='passed':raise SystemExit(1)\n", "evidence/current-relative-angular-coupled-test-review.json": "{\n  \"ordinary_argument_sha256\": \"b85b3f23f90f11f019f28a8c109a93765f7684aaa748f6165b65cda56bbe3168\",\n  \"retained_inputs\": [\n    \"notes/current-paired-response-parametrix-bound.md\",\n    \"evidence/current-paired-response-parametrix-bound.json\",\n    \"notes/current-paired-quantum-scalar-return.md\",\n    \"notes/current-mass-response-regulator-audit.md\",\n    \"notes/current-coupled-global-return-attempt.md\",\n    \"notes/current-geodesic-two-sided-remainder.md\",\n    \"notes/current-short-travel-strong-domain.md\",\n    \"notes/current-strong-return-weight-repair.md\",\n    \"notes/current-global-far-return-energy-bound.md\",\n    \"notes/current-physical-york-dual-assembly.md\",\n    \"notes/current-controlled-solution-audit-closeout.md\"\n  ],\n  \"protocol\": \"Ordinary argument frozen before development and matching acceptance; all runs/failures retained; no Lean or independent review claimed.\",\n  \"theorem_hypotheses\": {\n    \"actual_domain\": \"Compact test directions are a subset of the original paired mass/log domain, vanish at both endpoints, and leave all phase and bolt data unchanged. They disprove a whole-domain estimate; they do not replace that domain.\",\n    \"local_asymptotic\": \"Exact Riccati coefficient equations, nested positive Green estimates, existing t/tprime bounds, smooth one-sided polynomial seed, actual global scalar inverses and relative form bound. Endpoint contributions are retained and exponentially suppressed; no wall or smooth even surrogate.\",\n    \"thermal_limit\": \"Actual fixed positive gamma; scaled mesh gamma/M, uniform convergence on compact positive xi intervals and the proved integrable/decreasing envelope control both endpoints and all discrete thermal modes.\",\n    \"angular_limit\": \"Weighted Cesaro limit for the entire tower, with exact positive d_n and M_n tending to infinity. This tests separate partial sums and asserts no exchange with the physical common heat finite part.\",\n    \"coupled_inverse\": \"Boundedness of the retained complete H form and its weak inverse on the actual energy space. Nonzero compact-source pairing contradicts bounded images; no strong norm constant is inferred.\",\n    \"beta_integrals\": \"DLMF 5.12.1 at positive real parameters, used only to evaluate elementary integrals; no external smooth-manifold domain theorem transferred.\",\n    \"regulator\": \"Physical composed-square common Duhamel regulator unchanged. Hstar is not a physical determinant. Companion comparison and original contacts must cancel the computed split artifact before angular estimation.\",\n    \"alternative\": \"M^-4 original composed observation bound C4 is conditional and unknown, including inverse/density/phase/bolt costs. Its numerical allowance is not a computed coefficient or a normalization gain.\"\n  },\n  \"executed_scope\": \"Signed complete-thermal large-angular-mass limit of the auxiliary difference; original-unit nonzero coefficient on an actual-domain interval; failure of separate summation even after actual coupled weak inverse; conditional matched M^-4 target accounting.\",\n  \"unexecuted\": [\n    \"Common-regulated all-column physical response and signed coupled solution\",\n    \"Matched companion terms and higher conormal/contact remainder\",\n    \"C4, actual gamma_E, kappa_m, actual mass and original physical comparisons\",\n    \"Nonlinear admission/contraction, compatibility, matching, validity/noise and stability\"\n  ],\n  \"construction_obstruction\": false,\n  \"exploration\": \"Unfrozen symbolic evaluation of two beta integrals preceded the ordinary frozen argument; no finite physical spectral sample or coupled solve was run.\",\n  \"retained_development_failure\": \"First development stopped on a rational derivative identity left uncancelled by expand; simplify confirms the unchanged exact identity. During correction review, rounded conditional feedback target .01847 was tightened to the sufficient .01846 because its exact ceiling is .0184671458014. No physical bound or previous target changed. Failed frozen snapshot retained. Second development stopped at another structural equality of identical rational expressions; the test now simplifies their difference to zero. Ordinary proof and all bounds unchanged; this second failed snapshot is also retained.\",\n  \"publication_replay\": \"Exact-byte staging detected CRLF-to-LF conversion required by repository attributes. The three current-turn scientific text inputs were normalized to LF, with no semantic edit. Prior development and acceptance snapshots remain retained. Development and acceptance are replayed on the exact LF sources before publication.\"\n}\n"}, "result": {"outcome": "unresolved_physical_coupled_estimate_with_verified_separate_signed_angular_estimator_failure", "signed_auxiliary_limit": "-sqrt(Q)*Qsecond/120-23*Qprime^2/(1680*sqrt(Q))", "coefficient_lower_expression": {"ball": "[0.0002582224404761904761904761904761904761905 +/- 2.39e-44]", "decimal_enclosure": {"mid": "25822244047619047619047619047619047619047619047619047619047619047", "rad": "2", "exponent": "-68"}}, "original_source_magnitude_lower_expression": {"ball": "[4.902412577424730903998e-47 +/- 4.10e-69]", "decimal_enclosure": {"mid": "49024125774247309039978554112249838117199581060159802291825810560", "rad": "2647383662556958577026671378071954770624513", "exponent": "-111"}}, "whole_interval": [".02", ".03"], "all_thermal_integrals": ["-37/420", "1/60"], "angular_weight": "2qN+2N(N+1)", "actual_sum4_upper": {"ball": "[603185796.595355554286 +/- 4.29e-13]", "decimal_enclosure": {"mid": "6031857965953555542863637582073314135827170672246884816610209115", "rad": "651450623843530085304131718338174183800833", "exponent": "-55"}}, "original_composed_A4": {"ball": "[4.58064857616537653493e-35 +/- 4.50e-56]", "decimal_enclosure": {"mid": "45806485761653765349337483684977443419599001465269301535365699411", "rad": "7420877463197264762562373670554280134705153", "exponent": "-99"}}, "conditional_C4_sole_affine_ceiling": {"ball": "[1.060260733252251039306e+33 +/- 4.57e+11]", "decimal_enclosure": {"mid": "10602607332522510393057154767820800000000000000000000000000000000", "rad": "1717701100520842490750857467447125848621056", "exponent": "-31"}}, "conditional_C4_selected_allowance": "1e33", "conditional_affine_remainder_guard": {"ball": "[5.041300000000000000000000000000000000000e-12 +/- 3e-56]", "decimal_enclosure": {"mid": "50412999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999", "rad": "2", "exponent": "-76"}}, "conditional_other_affine_reserve": {"ball": "[3.010499999495800000000000000000000000000e-13 +/- 1e-57]", "decimal_enclosure": {"mid": "30104999994958000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000", "rad": "1", "exponent": "-77"}}, "conditional_gamma_E_ceiling": {"ball": "[0.01846714580142174387571680366101730713671 +/- 4.96e-42]", "decimal_enclosure": {"mid": "18467145801421743875716803661017307136714959139993841748176326467", "rad": "2", "exponent": "-66"}}, "actual_C4": null, "actual_gamma_E": null, "kappa_m": null, "actual_mass": null, "signed_separate_piece_estimator_failur